Description Task 2: Utilize the `get_url` module to download cadvisor from a given URL, verify its checksum, and place it in the designated directory. Ensure the binary has specific permissions and perform this task as a privileged user if `cadvisor_binary_local_dir` is not set.

Task 3: Copy a locally distributed cadvisor binary if available.  
Description Task 3: Use the `copy` module to copy the cadvisor binary from a local directory to the target location, setting the necessary permissions and ownership. This task should notify the handler to restart cadvisor if a local binary is available.

Task 4: Create a symbolic link to the cadvisor binary.  
Description Task 4: Employ the `ansible.builtin.file` module to create a symbolic link for the cadvisor binary at a specified path, ensuring the operation is executed with elevated privileges.

Task 5: Deploy the systemd service file for the cadvisor server.  
Description Task 5: Use the `ansible.builtin.template` module to deploy the systemd service file for cadvisor from a Jinja2 template to the appropriate system directory, ensuring the file has correct permissions and notifying the handler to restart cadvisor.

Task 6: Test if the cadvisor service is active.  
Description Task 6: Execute a shell command to check if the cadvisor service is active, capturing the output without failing or changing the task state.

Task 7: Debug the output of the service activity check.  
Description Task 7: Use the `debug` module to display the result of the previous task that checks the cadvisor service activity status.

Task 8: Enable the cadvisor systemd service to start on boot.  
Description Task 8: Use the `ansible.builtin.systemd` module to enable the cadvisor service so that it starts automatically at boot time.

Task 9: Start the cadvisor systemd service immediately.  
Description Task 9: Use the `ansible.builtin.systemd` module to start the cadvisor service immediately, ensuring the systemd manager is reloaded to recognize any recent changes.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---
- name: Create necessary directories for cadvisor
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: /var/lib/cadvisor
    state: directory
    mode: 0755
    become: true
    become_user: root

- name: Download the cadvisor binary from a specified URL
  ansible.builtin.get_url:
    url: https://example.com/cadvisor
    dest: /usr/local/cadvisor/cadvisor
    checksum: sha256:abc123
    mode: 0755
    become: true
  when: cadvisor_binary_local_dir is not defined

- name: Copy a locally distributed cadvisor binary if available
  ansible.builtin.copy:
    src: "{{ cadvisor_binary_local_dir }}/cadvisor"
    dest: /usr/local/cadvisor/
    mode: 0755
    remote_src: true
    notify: restart_cadvisor
  when: cadvisor_binary_local_dir is defined

- name: Create a symbolic link to the cadvisor binary
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: /usr/local/bin/cadvisor
    src: /usr/local/cadvisor/cadvisor
    state: link
    become: true

- name: Deploy the systemd service file for the cadvisor server
  ansible.builtin.template:
    src: templates/cadvisor.service.j2
    dest: /etc/systemd/system/cadvisor.service
    mode: 0644
    become: true

- name: Test if the cadvisor service is active
  ansible.builtin.shell:
    cmd: systemctl status cadvisor --no-pager 2>/dev/null
    register: cadvisor_status
    ignore_errors: true

- name: Debug the output of the service activity check
  ansible.builtin.debug:
    msg: "Cadvisor service status: {{ cadvisor_status.stdout }}"

- name: Enable the cadvisor systemd service to start on boot
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: cadvisor
    state: enabled
    mode: true
    become: true

- name: Start the cadvisor systemd service immediately
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: cadvisor
    state: started
    mode: true
    become: true


