 condition.\n\nNow, I\'ll adjust each task accordingly.\n\nFor the first task, I\'ll split the \'when\' into multiple lines.\n\nFor the other tasks, I\'ll change \'when: ...\' to a list under \'when:\'.\n\nLet me also check for any other potential issues, but the main errors are line length and truthy values in \'when\' clauses.\n\nSo, the corrected playbook should have each \'when\' clause as a list, and lines should be within 80 characters.\n</think>\n\n---\n\n- name: Disable swap if vault_hardening_disable_swap is set and swap is currently enabled.\n  shell: swapoff -a\n  args:\n    cmd: swapoff -a\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_disable_swap\n    - swap_output.stdout is defined\n  register: swap_output\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Remove swap entry from /etc/fstab\n  file:\n    path: /etc/fstab\n    state: absent\n    line: "^/dev/.* swap .*"\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_disable_swap\n\n- name: Set PAM limits to prevent core dumps\n  pam_limits:\n    limits:\n      core:\n        soft: -1\n        hard: -1\n        domain: all\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_disable_core_dumps\n\n- name: Create or modify script to disable history for vault commands\n  template:\n    src: vault_shell_history.sh.j2\n    dest: /etc/profile.d/vault_shell_history.sh\n    mode: \'755\'\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_disable_shell_command_history\n\n- name: Set SELinux to enforcing if enabled\n  shell: setenforce 1\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor\n    - ansible_selinux.enabled\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Check SELinux status\n  shell: sestatus\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor\n  changed_when: false\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Enforce AppArmor profile for Vault\n  shell: apparmorctl enforce /etc/apparmor.d/active.d/vault\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor\n    - ansible_apparmor.active\n  ignore_errors: yes' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '202