nes exceeding 80 characters and truncate them if necessary. However, from the provided playbook, it seems only the first line is too long.\n\nAfter making these changes, I\'ll ensure that the playbook structure remains valid, with each task correctly ordered and modules used as intended. I won\'t add or remove any tasks, just fix the syntax and formatting issues.\n\nFinally, I\'ll reconstruct the playbook with the corrected lines, ensuring that all tasks are present and functional, and that the YAML syntax is valid according to yamllint.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Disable swap if vault_hardening_disable_swap is set\n  shell: swapoff -a\n  args:\n    cmd: swapoff -a\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_disable_swap\n    - swap_output.stdout is defined\n  register: swap_output\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Remove swap entry from /etc/fstab\n  file:\n    path: /etc/fstab\n    state: absent\n    line: "^/dev/.* swap .*"\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_disable_swap\n\n- name: Set PAM limits to prevent core dumps\n  pam_limits:\n    limits:\n      core:\n        soft: -1\n        hard: -1\n        domain: all\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_disable_core_dumps\n\n- name: Create or modify script to disable history for vault commands\n  template:\n    src: vault_shell_history.sh.j2\n    dest: /etc/profile.d/vault_shell_history.sh\n    mode: \'755\'\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_disable_shell_command_history\n\n- name: Set SELinux to enforcing if enabled\n  shell: setenforce 1\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor\n    - ansible_selinux.enabled\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Check SELinux status\n  shell: sestatus\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor\n  changed_when: false\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Enforce AppArmor profile for Vault\n  shell: apparmorctl enforce /etc/apparmor.d/active.d/vault\n  when:\n    - vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor\n    - ansible_apparmor.active\n  ignore_errors: yes\n```' addition