, ensuring that each task uses the correct modules and parameters. I should also make sure that the playbook starts with \'---\' and is valid YAML.\n\nI think I\'ve covered all tasks. Let me make sure each task is in the right order and uses the correct modules. Also, the use of become is important for tasks that modify system files and packages.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Ensure the Docker apt key is removed from the trusted.gpg.d directory.\n  file:\n    path: /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/docker.gpg\n    state: absent\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Remove the old Docker apt source list from the sources.list.d directory.\n  file:\n    path: /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list\n    state: absent\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Uninstall obsolete Docker packages.\n  apt:\n    name:\n      - docker-engine\n      - docker-ce\n      - docker.io\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Remove the legacy Docker repository file.\n  file:\n    path: /etc/docker.repo\n    state: absent\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Install necessary dependencies for Docker.\n  apt:\n    state: present\n    update_cache: yes\n  command: apt-get update && apt-get install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificates curl software-properties-common\n\n- name: Add or remove the Docker repository based on a condition.\n  block:\n    - name: Remove Docker repo file if it exists\n      file:\n        path: /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list\n        state: absent\n      become: yes\n      notify: update_apt_cache\n    - name: Add Docker repo file if it doesn\'t exist\n      file:\n        path: /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list\n        state: present\n        content: \'deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/docker-archive-keyring.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu jammy stable\\n\'\n        create: yes\n        become: yes\n        notify: update_apt_cache\n  condition: "{{ docker_repo_exists | default(false) }}"\n\n- name: Flush handlers to update the apt cache immediately.\n  meta: