content='<think>\nAlright, let\'s break down how I approached creating the Ansible Playbook based on the user\'s instructions.\n\nFirst, I read the user\'s query carefully. They wanted a Playbook that strictly follows specific instructions, including starting with \'---\' and being structured for an Ansible Role under the tasks directory. They emphasized using the exact task names and modules, without adding or omitting anything.\n\nI started by understanding each task. Task 1 required importing assert.yml and running it once on localhost. I knew to use the import_tasks module with delegate_to set to localhost and run_once set to true.\n\nNext, Task 2 was about installing SELinux packages. I chose the apt module since it\'s suitable for Debian/Ubuntu systems, using the package manager to install from the variable selinux_requirements. Notifying the "Gather facts" handler made sense here.\n\nTask 3 needed to flush handlers, so I used the meta module\'s flush_handlers option. It\'s crucial for ensuring all notifications are processed.\n\nFor Task 4, I had to configure SELinux settings conditionally. The ansible_selinux.status fact and checking if the connection isn\'t a container were key conditions. Using the selinux module with state and policy variables, and notifying the "Reboot" handler upon success was the right approach.\n\nFinally, Task 5 involved managing SELinux booleans. I used import_tasks to include selinuxBOOLEIANS.yml, which iterates over each boolean, setting their values and persistence. Only running if selinux_booleans is defined was important.\n\nI made sure each task was in the correct order, modules were exact, and the structure adhered to Ansible\'s standards. I also avoided any extra comments or explanations, keeping it YAML clean as per the user\'s request.\n</think>\n\n```\n---\n- name: Import the assert.yml tasks file to verify prerequisites\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Install the required SELinux packages\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ selinux_requirements }}"\n    state: present\n  notify: Gather facts\n\n- name: Flush the handlers to ensure all notifications are processed\n  meta: flush_handlers\n\n- name: Configure SELinux settings\n  ansible.posix.selinux:\n    state: "{{ selinux_state }}"\n    policy: "{{ selinux_policy }}"\n    set enforcement: yes\n  when:\n    - ansible_selinux.status is defined\n    - ansible_connection != "docker"\n    - ansible_connection != "lxc"\n  notify: Reboot\n\n- name: Manage SELinux booleans\n  import_tasks: selinuxBOOLEIANS.yml\n  when: selinux_booleans is defined\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-14T09:46:30.911291031Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 8284112677, 'load_duration': 96847615, 'prompt_eval_count': 563, 'prompt_eval_duration': 247505709, 'eval_count': 553, 'eval_duration': 7938301684, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--aa35f4d4-9b11-4bd5-9ae3-9a34ee1b83e8-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 563, 'output_tokens': 553, 'total_tokens': 1116}
