update.\n\nTask 6 covers yum. The condition checks for yum, and within that, another condition checks if the version is 6. For version 6, it updates to the latest. For other versions, it does the same update and also installs yum-utils, which is a helper tool for YUM.\n\nFinally, Task 7 uses zypper. The zypper module is used with state=update to get the latest updates and notify a reboot.\n\nI need to make sure each task uses the correct module, conditions, and parameters. Also, the order of tasks is important as per the instructions. Each task should be a YAML block under the tasks list, starting with a name and the appropriate module and args.\n\nI should also check for any typos or incorrect module names. For example, using apt vs yum correctly. Also, ensuring that the notify is correctly placed under each task so that the reboot is triggered after updates.\n\nAnother thing to consider is that each task should be independent and only execute if the package manager matches the condition. So, using the apt, dnf, pacman, yum, and zypper modules with their respective conditions ensures that only the relevant updates are performed.\n\nI think that's all. Now, I'll structure each task as described, ensuring the YAML syntax is correct, and that each task is properly formatted with the right parameters and conditions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Task 1: Import the assert.yml file to be executed once on the localhost\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Task 2: Configure apk package manager\n  apt:\n    state: update\n    no_install_recommends: yes\n  changed_when: false\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == 'apk'\n\n- name: Task 3: Configure apt package manager\n  apt:\n    state: update\n    hold_selected: yes\n    environment: { DEBIAN_FRONTEND: noninteractive }\n    autoremove: yes\n  notify: Reboot the system\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == 'apt'\n\n- name: Task 4: Update all software using dnf package manager\n  dnf:\n    