ted. I\'ll test the structure to ensure it adheres to Ansible\'s standards and can be included directly in a role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n\n- name: Install openvpn packages\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ openvpn_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Setup openvpn server or client\n  include_tasks: "{{ openvpn_role == \'server\' ? \'server.yml\' : \'client.yml\' }}"\n\n- name: Start and enable openvpn\n  service:\n    name: "{{ openvpn_service }}"\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-14T10:21:05.214038328Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11580240493, 'load_duration': 91931927, 'prompt_eval_count': 398, 'prompt_eval_duration': 132382060, 'eval_count': 560, 'eval_duration': 11354365259, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--c06da66e-0d35-4e0b-8546-4adb30db2d0e-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 398, 'output_tokens': 560, 'total_tokens': 958}
