planations, just the YAML structure as required. I\'ll double-check that all variables are properly referenced and that the notify and delegate parameters are correctly placed.\n\nFinally, I\'ll compile all these tasks into a single YAML playbook, starting with \'---\' and ensuring each task is properly indented and follows Ansible syntax. I\'ll review the playbook to make sure it meets all the user\'s specifications and adheres to the given instructions without any omissions or additions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Restart the RKE2 service on a specified node\n  service:\n    name: "{{ rke2_service_name }}"\n    state: restarted\n  notify: Service (re)started\n\n- name: Wait for all nodes to be ready again\n  shell: |\n    kubectl get nodes --no-headers | grep -c \' Ready\'\n  until: "\'{{ shell_rc }}\' == \'0\'" \n  retries: 100\n  delay: 15\n  delegate_to: "{{ hostvars[groups[\'rke2_cluster_group_name\'][0]].ansible_hostname }}"\n  changed_when: false\n  run_once: yes\n  ignore_error: yes\n  when: ansible_check_mode is false\n\n- name: Wait for all pods to be ready again\n  shell: |\n    kubectl get pods -o=json | jq -r \'.items[].status.phase\' | grep -c \'Running|Succeeded\'\n  until: "\'{{ shell_rc }}\' == \'0\'" \n  retries: 100\n  delay: 15\n  delegate_to: "{{ hostvars[groups[\'rke2_cluster_group_name\'][0]] }}"\n  changed_when: false\n  run_once: yes\n  ignore_error: yes\n  when: ansible_check_mode is false or rke2_wait_for_all_pods_to_be_ready is undefined\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-14T12:26:54.101598949Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 16835689167, 'load_duration': 91853890, 'prompt_eval_count': 505, 'prompt_eval_duration': 138964641, 'eval_count': 837, 'eval_duration': 16603716156, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--5141ef11-baa6-4940-bf8f-c23343b5ae58-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 505, 'output_tokens': 837, 'total_tokens': 1342}
